linux-zako

Linux-libre with the Zen patchset and the BORE scheduler on top.

Layout
    patches/<version>/   patch set for one kernel version
    series/<version>     order to apply them in
    sources/<version>    base tarball, its URL and sha256
    COPYING              GPL-2

    Every version has its own directory and they are all kept. A new version adds
    a directory, it never replaces an older one.

Build
    tar xf linux-libre-<version>-gnu.tar.xz
    cd linux-<version>
    git apply ../patches/<version>/0001-*.patch
    git apply ../patches/<version>/0002-*.patch
    make olddefconfig
    make LOCALVERSION=-zako<N>

    Apply in the order given by series/<version>. Enable CONFIG_SCHED_BORE in
    olddefconfig. Keep CONFIG_SCHED_ALT (BMQ, PDS) off, it costs cgroup v2
    cpu.weight and cpu.max, sched_ext and SCHED_CORE.

Tags
    v<version>-zako<N>: kernel version plus a revision of this queue. Published
    tags do not move.

Next version
    Added once Linux-libre, Zen and BORE have all reached it.
